  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Evaluation, identification and formulation of a post-AUSP IV institutional support programme to the AU - Extension</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The contract is contributing to the successful implementation of the AU-EU partnership priorities and of the AU institutional reform and Agenda 2063 and reinforce the institutional and operational capacity of the AU. For this purpose, the implementation should ensure close and constant coordination with the AUC relevant offices, and other relevant AU bodies, such as but not limited to Africa CFTA Secretariat, AUDA/NEPAD, Africa CDC and stakeholders. In coordination and under the leadership of the EU Delegation to AU team, involvement of the AU JFA partners should be ensured in the implementation of the specific objective. The following components should be part of the assignment:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;a) Assessment of the AUSP impact and lessons learned:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Provide an assessment of the implementation of the current AUSP IV programme&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Identify the key lessons learned and challenges of the previous programmes&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Mapping key actors involved in the AUSP&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Mapping other international stakeholders working on institutional support and supporting the AU budget&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;b)&amp;nbsp;Identification and formulation of a post-AUSP IV institutional support programme to the AU&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
